        <body>
            <div xml:id="d467">

                <pb facs="0850" n="788" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg788"/>

                <head>No. 462.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Reed
                        to Mr. Evarts.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-04-27"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 27, 1878</date>.
                        (Received May 18.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 8.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Gaceta of this morning publishes a law
                    fixing the permanent force of the army in the Peninsula for the economical year
                    of 1878 to 1879 at 100,000 men.</p>
                <p>By this law, a copy and translation of which are hereto annexed, you will observe
                    that the army in the island of Cuba is to be of such force as shall be deemed
                    necessary to complete the pacification of the island.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>DWIGHT T. REED.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d467-a1.xml" xpointer="d467-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
